[Slide 1]
Before a project starts, how do you actually know someone will deliver what they promised? 
That’s the gap Deadline is built to close—making professional reliability measurable, verifiable, and portable.

[Slide 2]
Right now, trust breaks on both sides.
Clients rely on scattered references and gut feel, slowing down hiring. 
Providers struggle to prove what they delivered and face unclear terms and delayed payments. 
To see how deep this friction runs, the Economic Survey 2025–26 estimates ₹8.1 lakh crore is locked in delayed MSME payments, 
and 2,56,892 applications were filed on MSME Samadhaan up to 31 December 2025. 
That isn’t our addressable market—it’s the economic backdrop of what happens when commitments aren’t clear.

[Slide 3]
Deadline introduces one portable layer of trust: a Deadline ID and Trust Passport that travel with you. 
It brings five elements together: Verified Identity through trusted sources, Agreed Commitments on scope and timelines, 
timestamped Delivery Evidence, Two-Sided Reputation tied to real engagements, 
and optional Payment Protection enabled through appropriately regulated partners.

[Slide 4]
The workflow turns a promise into proof in four steps. 
First, both parties agree on scope, deliverables, and deadlines. 
Second, they track milestones and submit evidence in real time. 
Third, they record approval—or resolve disputes transparently. 
Fourth, that verified outcome updates the portable Trust Passport.

[Slide 5]
We’re moving professional relationships from scattered reviews, unverifiable claims, 
and one-platform reputations—to structured commitments, evidence-backed outcomes, 
and two-sided accountability you actually own. A trust layer built to work across platforms. 
Deadline: Trust. Commit. Deliver.
